course: dictionary
lesson: 2960
title: Droop: hanging down or feeling low
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Droop is a word you can often see. Something that droops hangs or bends down, usually because it is weak, tired or has no water. «The flowers drooped in the heat» shows plants that have gone limp and floppy in hot weather.
explain: Droop can also describe feelings. «His spirits drooped» does not mean anything is hanging down. It means he suddenly felt sad or lost his energy. The words around it, like spirits, tell you that the meaning is about mood.
explain: «The dog's tail drooped» is not just about a tail moving down: it shows the dog is sad or tired. Ask yourself: is something physically hanging, or is someone feeling low? That question helps you choose the right meaning.
fact: Droop is a verb: droop, droops, drooped, drooping. It can also be a noun: a droop is a downward bend or slope.
fact: «Drooped» means hung or bent down because of being weak, tired or without water.
fact: In science, a plant without water droops because its cells lose water and it cannot stay stiff.
fact: In stories, «drooping eyelids» show tiredness, and «a drooping head» can show sadness.
fact: In art, drooping describes shapes that sag.
exercise: «The flowers drooped in the heat.» What does drooped mean here? | Blew away in the wind | Grew very tall and bright | Sang loudly to the sun | *Hung down because they were weak and dry
exercise: «His spirits drooped.» What does drooped suggest? | He jumped up and cheered | He bent down to tie his shoe | *He became sad or lost his energy | He grew a lot taller
exercise: «The roof had a droop in the middle.» What is a droop here? | *A downward bend or slope | A bright colour | A kind of bird | A loud noise
test: Which sentence shows a plant that needs water? | The lettuce was chopped into small pieces | The lettuce shone brightly in the sun | *The lettuce drooped after a week with no water | The lettuce was sold at the market
test: «Her eyelids were drooping during the long lesson.» What does this most likely show? | She was very angry | She was winning the game | *She was tired | She was cold and wet
exam: In a story, «his head drooped», what is the best meaning? | He was reading a map | He was running very fast | He was dancing with joy | *He looked sad or defeated
